From 533640bbf363861023c0050a91a53a6d6aa59b1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: robbertuittenbroek <robbert.uittenbroek@rijksoverheid.nl>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:29:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] fix: stop the watches of a removed namespace after a full
 sync

RemoveNamespace cancels the watches it finds in apiMeta.namespaceCancels, but only the incremental add (syncNamespaceResources) registered a per-namespace cancel there. sync() and startMissingWatches started every namespaced watch on the API-wide context, so after a full sync RemoveNamespace found nothing to cancel. The watches of the removed namespace kept running, and once the namespace was deleted every list and watch on it returned 403 (the controller's RoleBinding went with it). watchEvents only stops on 404, so it retried every watchResourcesRetryTimeout per API type until the next full resync, which saturated the client-side rate limiter and starved the incremental add of new namespaces.

- Every path that starts a namespaced watch now derives a per-namespace context through apiMeta.namespaceWatchContext, which registers its cancel and cancels a previous one for the same namespace (a re-added namespace leaked its old watch before).
- Safety net: watchEvents stops instead of retrying when its namespace is no longer managed, and a 404 for such a namespace no longer drops the whole GVK through stopWatching.
- RemoveNamespace logs "Stop syncing namespace" with the number of stopped watches.

Tests: watches of a namespace from a full sync and from an incremental add go quiet after RemoveNamespace; an unmanaged namespace's watch stops on 403 and keeps the GVK on 404; re-registering cancels the previous context. TestSync_SyncWarnings_ResetBetweenSyncs now changes the namespaces under the lock, because the watches of its first sync read them.
